A posting some time back has confused many people who wanted to
run PCNETHACK2.3.  The posting states that you should
set TERMCAP to point to a directory containing TERMCAP.CNF.

This is erroneous (at least it doesn't work on any of our systems)

What you really do follows:

Take the file TERMCAP from either NHACKSUP.ARC or your old
version of NetHack, or some other termcap based program.

Place TERMCAP in some directory.  Any directory.

Now look at the pathname of TERMCAP (e.g. \ETC\TERMCAP).
Replace backslashes (\) by foreslashes (/).

Enter this DOS command:
  SET TERMCAP=/dir1/dir2/.../dirn/TERMCAP
e.g. SET TERMCAP=/ETC/TERMCAP.
Better put this in your AUTOEXEC.BAT file.

Then:  set TERM as described by many posters.  The only real
problem seems to be the posting that mentioned a fictitious
file by the name of TERMCAP.CNF.


